### Page 1 of 4

```text
Page 1 of 4
CONTRACT NO.________
AGREEMENT BETWEEN THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
AND LARAMIE COUNTY
FOR ANIMAL CONTROL SERVICES

1. Parties. The parties to this Agreement are the City of Cheyenne, a municipality duly
organized and existing under the laws of the State of Wyoming, hereafter “City,” who
address is 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001, and Laramie County, a
county government organized and existing under the laws of the State of Wyoming,
hereafter “County,” who address is 310 West 19th Street, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.
2. Purpose of Agreement.  The purpose of this Agreement is to authorize the City to furnish
the County with Animal Control services as set forth in this Agreement.
3. Term:  This Agreement is effective upon approval and execution by the parties.  The term
of this Agreement shall be from September 1, 2021 through June 30, 2022.  The parties
may, by mutual agreement, renew this Agreement for additional one-year terms, through
an amendment reflecting then-current payment and any other relevant changes.
4. Payment:  The County agrees to pay the following amount for Animal Control services
described herein.
a. The County shall pay upon receipt of the City’s invoice, for Animal Control
expenses only, the monthly amount of $10,900.00 for each of the months of
September 1, 2021 through June 30, 2022.
b. In no event shall the amount paid under this Agreement exceed $109,000.00.
c. The County shall furnish use of the Laramie County Combined Communications
Center (LCCCC) as a component of this agreement.  Consideration for this
service is reflected in the agreed upon pricing detailed above.  Such use shall be
limited to calls regarding animal control responsibilities detailed in Section 5 of
this Agreement received by LCCCC and calls received by LCCCC where Animal
Control is needed to support a law enforcement or other public safety agency.
The City shall provide Animal Control with their own radios; the County will not
provide any radio equipment to the City as part of this agreement.
5. City’s Responsibilities.
a. The City shall operate Animal Control for both the City of Cheyenne and the
unincorporated areas of Laramie County.  All Animal Control operations in
unincorporated areas of Laramie County shall be conducted in conformance with
any applicable Wyoming state law as it may change from time to time and the
Laramie County Rabies Control District, Animal Control District and Animal
Control Regulations, Adopted July 20th, 2004 (Hereinafter the “Laramie County
regulations”).
b. Such operations shall include, but not be limited to the following:
By Stefanie Boster at 11:03 am, May 04, 2022
```

### Page 2 of 4

```text
Page 2 of 4
i. Capture of Animals: Animal Control will provide humane and safe animal
capture services for stray dogs and cats found within the limits of Laramie
County and shall transport them to the Cheyenne Animal Shelter.
ii. Public Nuisance Complaint Calls: Animal Control will respond to public
nuisance complaint calls as provided by the Laramie County Regulations.
iii. Animals Running At Large: Animal Control will respond to Animals
Running At Large as provided by the Laramie County Regulations.
iv. Vicious or Dangerous Dogs: Animal Control shall respond to complaints
relating to vicious or dangerous dogs as provided for by applicable law or
regulation.
c. It shall be the City’s responsibility to hire, train and manage all Animal Control
personnel and officers who shall operate within the City of Cheyenne and the
unincorporated areas of Laramie County.
d. The City shall furnish to the County, through the Director of Compliance,
monthly reports reflecting such Animal Control statistics as are collected under
industry best practices. The report shall also include a description of any
complaints made regarding Animal Control services and the resolution of those
complaints and any public education programs conducted within that month.
e. The City shall perform operation of Animal Control in line with industry best
practices and shall maintain the professional and organizational integrity
expected of an organization engaged in providing animal control services.
6. County’s Responsibilities.
a. The County shall make payment as specified in this Agreement.
b. The County shall promptly report any concerns or complaints received about
Animal Control services directly to the City, Attention: Director of Compliance.
7. Responsibilities of Both Parties.
a. Establish and maintain records documenting calls and investigations conducted
by Animal Control officers including, but not limited to, records of complaints
received and the resolution of each complaint.
8. General Provisions.
a. Amendments.  Any changes, modifications, revisions, or amendment to this
Agreement, which are mutually agreed upon by the Parties to this Agreement
shall be incorporated by written instrument, executed, and signed by all Parties to
this Agreement.
b. Applicable Law. The construction, interpretation, and enforcement of this
Agreement shall be governed by the laws of the State of Wyoming.  The courts
of the State of Wyoming shall have jurisdiction over this Agreement and the
Parties, and the venue shall be in the First Judicial District, Laramie County,
Wyoming.
c. Compliance with the Laws. The City and County shall keep informed of and
comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations, and
industry standards in the performance of this Agreement.
```

### Page 3 of 4

```text
Page 3 of 4
d. Entirety of Agreement.  This Agreement, consisting of four (4) pages, represents
the entire and integrated agreement between the Parties and supersedes all prior
negotiations, representations, and agreements, whether written or oral.
e. Indemnification.  Each Party to this Agreement shall assume the risk of any
liability arising from its own conduct.  Neither Party agrees to insure or indemnify
the other.
f. Notice. All notices arising out of or from the provisions of this Agreement shall
be in writing and given to the Parties either by regular mail or delivery in person.
g. Nondiscrimination. The City and County shall comply with the Civil Rights Act
of 1964, the Wyoming Fair Employment Practices Act, Wyo. Stat. § 27-9-105, et
seq., and the Americans with Disabilities Act (AD)), as amended, 42 U.S.C. §
12101, et seq.  The City and County shall assure that no person is subjected to
discrimination because of age, sex, race, religion, national origin, or disability in
connection with the performance of this Agreement.
h. Prior Approval.  This Agreement shall not be binding upon either party, no
services shall be performed under the terms of this Agreement, nor shall payment
be made until this Agreement and been reduced to writing and approval by all
necessary authorities.
i. Governmental Immunity. Nothing in this Agreement shall be deemed to have
waived the City or County’s governmental immunity, as provided by any
applicable law including Wyo. Stat. § 1-39-101, et seq.  Further, the City and
County fully retain all immunities and defenses provided by law with regard to
any action, whether in tort, contract, or any other theory of law, based on this
Agreement.
j. Termination.  The County may terminate this Agreement for cause immediately
without notice or liability in the event the City fails to perform.  Either Party may
terminate this Agreement without cause upon sixty (60) days written notice.
k. Signatures.  In witness thereof, the parties to this Agreement, through their duly
authorized representatives, have executed this Agreement on the days and dates
set out below and certify that they have read, understood, and agreed to the terms
and conditions of this Agreement.

Rest of Page Intentionally Left Blank

CONTRACT NO.________
AGREEMENT BETWEEN THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
AND LARAMIE COUNTY
```

